      "Language": "hun",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Obstructive sleep apnea syndrome is a common disorder in adults associated with several cardiovascular diseases and impaired quality of life. Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease is also a common clinical condition in middle-aged adults. The combination of these two conditions can eventuate a severe combined sleep-related breathing disorder. It is important to recognize coexisting sleep apnea in patients with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease in time and to treat it appropriately."},
